From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 07:45:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02300/11362] [outer-loop] FIX gap-fill generation:
 delta-compress prompt (18k->6.6k) + provide WIN as a global

Root cause of all prior gap-fill failures was NOT output max_tokens (the
model emitted only ~385 tokens, stopped_limit=None). Two real issues:
 (1) the cn04 gap-fill prompt (18245 chars ~23k tok) OVERFLOWED the 16384
     context -> input truncated=True, so the model never saw the contract;
 (2) when the prompt DID fit, the model HARDCODED the entire 64x64 win
     grid as a numpy literal -> output overflow.
Fix: _compact_gap_prompt_grids (WIN state + a few capped deltas, 18k->6.6k)
AND provide WIN + np as GLOBALS in the exec scope + the saved heuristic so
the model writes a tiny function that REFERENCES WIN instead of emitting it.
RESULT (validated, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B on the iGPU): emits a valid
'def goal_distance(grid): return float((grid != WIN).sum())',
goal_distance(win)=0.0, goal_distance(start)=3983.0.
Generation is FIXED. Remaining blocker is the search ENGINE (v3 cannot
solve cn04 regardless); next target is a game+engine combo where a
heuristic provably helps (lp85 OfflineSolver / heuristic-guided v2).
